1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:02,000
Same order, three ways.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Two of these are wrong for your category.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:06,800
Polybag. Cheapest, thinnest, fastest to pack.

4
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:08,600
Fine for a T-shirt.

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:12,000
Useless for anything that leaks, breaks, or has a hard edge.

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,800
Padded mailer. Some cushioning, some structure.

7
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:17,200
Good for most soft goods and small electronics.

8
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:20,000
Still won't survive a real drop with anything glass or ceramic.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:23,200
Box. Rigid, heaviest, most expensive.

10
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:27,000
The only one of the three that protects a shape, not just a surface.

11
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,000
Pick by category, not by habit.

12
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Cosmetics in a polybag is how you get a refund request.

13
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:33,000
A book in a box is how you overpay on every order.

14
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Which one are you actually using?

